<title>PHILIPPINES: PCIBank predicts sharply higher '97 net.</title>
<headline>PCIBank predicts sharply higher '97 net.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Commercial International Bank (PCIBank), one of the country's largest commercial banks, on Thursday predicted a sharp increase in net income this year after a rise in first quarter figures.</p>
<p>Bank president, Rafael Buenaventura, told reporters first quarter net rose to one billion pesos from 684.5 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>He targetted net income for the year at 4.0 billion pesos against 2.99 billion last year.</p>
</text>
